# Copy to .env.local for development, and add the same keys in your host's
# dashboard for production. All are optional — the site builds and runs
# without them, it just degrades gracefully.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed once you point a custom domain at the site. On Vercel this is
# detected automatically, so leave it blank until you have your own domain.
#
# It matters because link previews (the card X, Telegram and LinkedIn show)
# require an ABSOLUTE image URL. Get this wrong and the preview silently
# disappears. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub contribution graph
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this the Signal section shows a seeded placeholder grid and labels
# itself "sample data". With it, the graph is your real contribution calendar.
#
# GitHub's REST API does not expose the contribution calendar; only GraphQL
# does, and it requires auth even for public data. Hence the token.
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   Classic token  -> tick the `read:user` scope, nothing else.
#   Fine-grained   -> read-only access to your own profile is enough.
# Never commit the real value.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form email
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this, /api/contact still validates and rate-limits, but only logs the
# message to the server console. See the TODO in src/app/api/contact/route.ts.
RESEND_API_KEY=
